Band Description: Formed by Arthur "Blower" Vance (a 52-year-old former shipyard welder who plays a dented 1950s contra-tuba wrapped in electrical tape) and Maya Lin (a 19-year-old cassette DJ and synth collector), The Portbury Float Association bridge generations with gleeful ferocity. Onstage, Vance stands front and center in grease-smudged denim overalls, huffing lung-collapsing sub-bass riffs that vibrate audience ribcages, while Lin operates a bank of gleaming 1980s rackmount gear and DX keyboards clad in an oversized electric-pink waterproof jacket. Backed by two energetic percussionists drumming on upturned plastic chemical drums and a four-piece brass choir, their live sets feel less like a downbeat club night and more like a riotous seaside carnival parade erupting out of an industrial shipyard.
