Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Crown Glass Swallows the Tide
- Story & Context: On a sodden October dawn in 1987, Maya Lin dragged an extension cord through the mud of Avonmouth Dock to power Arthur Vance’s antique contra-tuba inside a derelict bottleworks kiln. When the passing Liberian cargo vessel Nordic Trader groaned an immense low-F fog signal into the grey estuary, Arthur instinctively blasted back with a euphoric three-note major rip that sent vibrating shards of green bottle glass dancing across the concrete floor. Dock security sprinted across the slipway brandishing flashlights, only to stop dead as sixty night-shift warehousemen began skanking along to the SP-1200's cheerful 96-BPM breakbeat. Above the clattering machinery, Arthur raised his megaphone and barked the hook that launched the whole movement: "Blow the horn bright, boys, daylight won't wait!"
