Track 2: Vance’s Annealing Shed
- Story & Context: Huddled inside the drafty corrugated kiln shed off Royal Portbury Dock, Arthur confessed to Maya that his lungs were giving out from thirty years of dockyard welding, his breath smelling of stale tobacco and boiled lemon sweets. Between frantic sips of hot cider, he spent four grueling hours tracking basslines on his dented BBb horn, fighting through a leaking spit valve to match the rhythmic three-blast greeting of an incoming freighter anchored in the foggy roadstead. A fierce argument flared when Maya pitched his brass up an entire octave through an 80s pitch-shifter to make the groove bounce like a seaside carnival, causing Arthur to slam his wrench down in fury before breaking into a wheezing, toothy laugh. That giddy compromise birthed the EP’s emotional centerpiece, driven by a joyous group-sung hook: "Melt down the sorrow and blow me the morning bell."
